{"title":"Career roadmap · Researcher","role":"Researcher","summary":"A Researcher investigates questions systematically, evaluates evidence, develops arguments, analyses information and communicates findings through reports, papers, presentations or other scholarly outputs.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"A Researcher investigates questions systematically, evaluates evidence, develops arguments, analyses information and communicates findings through reports, papers, presentations or other scholarly outputs."},{"type":"p","text":"For a BA Philosophy graduate, the most natural research strengths are critical thinking, logic, argument analysis, ethics, epistemology, political philosophy, conceptual analysis and academic writing. However, “Researcher” is a broad career rather than a single profession. The student should ideally develop a research domain alongside philosophy."},{"type":"p","text":"Strong combinations include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Philosophy + Ethics"},{"text":"Philosophy + Political Science"},{"text":"Philosophy + Public Policy"},{"text":"Philosophy + Psychology"},{"text":"Philosophy + Economics"},{"text":"Philosophy + AI/Ethics"},{"text":"Philosophy + Law"},{"text":"Philosophy + Digital Humanities"},{"text":"Philosophy + Education"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest long-term route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Philosophy","Research Methods","Domain Specialisation","Research Internship","MA/PG","Research Assistant/Analyst","Researcher","Specialist/Research Lead"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Undergraduate"},{"text":"Research Intern, Research Volunteer"},{"text":"Literature review and data collection"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Research Assistant, Junior Research Analyst"},{"text":"Research support and analysis"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Research Associate, Research Analyst"},{"text":"Independent research components"}],[{"text":"Specialist"},{"text":"Policy Researcher, Ethics Researcher, Social Researcher"},{"text":"Domain-specific research"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"Senior Research Associate, Senior Researcher"},{"text":"Research projects and publications"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Research Lead, Project Research Manager"},{"text":"Research strategy and teams"}],[{"text":"Academic"},{"text":"Lecturer/Research Scholar/Professor"},{"text":"Teaching and scholarly research"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Research Director, Centre/Program Head"},{"text":"Research portfolio and institutional strategy"}],[{"text":"Independent"},{"text":"Research Consultant"},{"text":"Independent studies and advisory work"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During BA Philosophy","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Philosophical & Analytical Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Core areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Introduction to philosophy"},{"text":"Logic"},{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Epistemology"},{"text":"Metaphysics"},{"text":"Political philosophy"},{"text":"Philosophy of science"},{"text":"Indian philosophy"},{"text":"Western philosophy"},{"text":"Philosophy of language"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Develop these abilities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Critical reading"},{"text":"Argument identification"},{"text":"Logical reasoning"},{"text":"Conceptual analysis"},{"text":"Evidence evaluation"},{"text":"Structured writing"},{"text":"Debate"},{"text":"Academic discussion"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Learn to distinguish"},{"type":"h","text":"Claim"},{"type":"flow","items":["Evidence","Reasoning","Counterargument","Conclusion"]},{"type":"p","text":"This structure is fundamental to professional research."},{"type":"h","text":"Year-1 project"},{"type":"h","text":"Critical Analysis Research Paper"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose a question such as:"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Can artificial intelligence make ethical decisions?\""},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research question"},{"text":"Existing viewpoints"},{"text":"Arguments"},{"text":"Counterarguments"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Analysis"},{"text":"Conclusion"},{"text":"References"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Research Methodology"},{"type":"p","text":"Move beyond philosophical essays into formal research."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn research methods"},{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative methods"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"Case studies"},{"text":"Thematic analysis"},{"text":"Content analysis"},{"text":"Discourse analysis"},{"text":"Document analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative foundations"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Basic statistical inference"},{"text":"Data visualisation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Academic research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature reviews"},{"text":"Research questions"},{"text":"Hypothesis development"},{"text":"Conceptual frameworks"},{"text":"Citation"},{"text":"Bibliographies"},{"text":"Academic databases"},{"text":"Research ethics"},{"text":"Plagiarism prevention"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research tools"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Zotero"},{"text":"Mendeley"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Google Sheets"},{"text":"Survey tools"},{"text":"NVivo/qualitative-analysis concepts"},{"text":"SPSS/R/Python basics depending on research area"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year-2 project"},{"type":"h","text":"Systematic Literature Review"},{"type":"p","text":"Select a topic and produce:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research question"},{"text":"Search strategy"},{"text":"Source-selection criteria"},{"text":"Literature matrix"},{"text":"Thematic analysis"},{"text":"Research gaps"},{"text":"Future research directions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Choose a Research Specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the most important decision for employability."},{"type":"h","text":"1. Ethics Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Applied ethics"},{"text":"Bioethics"},{"text":"Business ethics"},{"text":"AI ethics"},{"text":"Technology ethics"},{"text":"Research ethics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ethics Researcher"},{"text":"AI Ethics Research Assistant"},{"text":"Research Associate"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Political & Public Policy Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Political philosophy"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Public policy"},{"text":"Institutions"},{"text":"Public administration"},{"text":"Policy evaluation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy Research Assistant"},{"text":"Policy Researcher"},{"text":"Governance Researcher"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Social Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Social statistics"},{"text":"Survey research"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Social policy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Social Research Assistant"},{"text":"Social Researcher"},{"text":"Research Analyst"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. AI & Technology Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Combine philosophy with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI ethics"},{"text":"Responsible AI"},{"text":"AI governance"},{"text":"Technology policy"},{"text":"Algorithmic fairness"},{"text":"Human-AI interaction"},{"text":"Digital ethics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python basics"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Machine-learning concepts"},{"text":"AI fundamentals"},{"text":"Research methodology"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI Ethics Research Assistant"},{"text":"Responsible AI Researcher"},{"text":"AI Governance Research Analyst"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Philosophy of Science"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Scientific reasoning"},{"text":"Philosophy of science"},{"text":"Scientific methodology"},{"text":"Technology and society"},{"text":"Evidence and uncertainty"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential pathways:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Science policy"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Technology policy"},{"text":"Academic research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Education Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Philosophy of education"},{"text":"Education policy"},{"text":"Learning science"},{"text":"Pedagogy"},{"text":"Educational assessment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Education Research Assistant"},{"text":"Education Policy Researcher"},{"text":"Education Programme Researcher"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Independent Research"},{"type":"p","text":"For a 4-year Honours pathway, develop the ability to execute a complete research project."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced literature review"},{"text":"Research design"},{"text":"Data collection"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Academic publication"},{"text":"Conference presentations"},{"text":"Research ethics"},{"text":"Grant/proposal writing"},{"text":"Research communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the research domain:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"SPSS"},{"text":"R"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"NVivo/qualitative analysis"},{"text":"GIS"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A humanities researcher does not need to learn every tool. Select tools according to the research question."},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Research Project"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended project"},{"type":"note","label":"AI Ethics and Society","text":"A Multidisciplinary Research Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible research questions:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Can AI systems make ethically defensible decisions?"},{"text":"How should algorithmic bias be evaluated?"},{"text":"Who should be accountable for AI-generated decisions?"},{"text":"What principles should govern AI in education?"},{"text":"How does AI change human autonomy?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research structure"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Question"},{"type":"h","text":"Literature Review"},{"type":"h","text":"Conceptual Framework"},{"type":"h","text":"Methodology"},{"type":"h","text":"Evidence/Data"},{"type":"h","text":"Analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Counterarguments"},{"type":"h","text":"Findings"},{"type":"h","text":"Conclusion"},{"type":"h","text":"References"},{"type":"h","text":"4-Year Honours / Honours with Research"},{"type":"p","text":"The additional year can be used for a substantial research dissertation."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI ethics"},{"text":"Bioethics"},{"text":"Political philosophy"},{"text":"Public policy"},{"text":"Philosophy of science"},{"text":"Philosophy of technology"},{"text":"Social justice"},{"text":"Environmental ethics"},{"text":"Business ethics"},{"text":"Digital ethics"},{"text":"Philosophy of education"},{"text":"Indian philosophy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research outputs to target"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, ideally have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"1 substantial dissertation"},{"text":"2–3 research papers"},{"text":"1 conference presentation"},{"text":"Research portfolio"},{"text":"Literature-review project"},{"text":"Data-analysis project"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Publication in a peer-reviewed journal is valuable but should never be treated as guaranteed or pursued through questionable/predatory journals."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation Options"},{"type":"table","header":["Specia